# HTML prototype standards

Apply when creating or editing design request HTML canvas artifacts.

## File requirements

- **Self-contained:** Single `.html` file with inline `<style>`; avoid external CSS/JS dependencies in MVP.
- **No build step:** Designer opens file or canvas preview directly in Cursor.
- **Version header:** HTML comment block with prototype name, semver, and changelog line.

## Mobile-first viewport

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
```

- Design width: **390px** (iPhone 14/15 baseline) unless brief specifies otherwise.
- Center frame on larger viewports with neutral background (`#f5f5f5` or similar).
- Use `max-width: 390px; margin: 0 auto; min-height: 100dvh;` on root app container.

## Safe areas

```css
padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top, 0);
padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0);
padding-left: env(safe-area-inset-left, 0);
padding-right: env(safe-area-inset-right, 0);
```

- Reserve **~34px** bottom inset for home indicator on primary CTAs.
- Status bar region: avoid critical content under notch; use top padding ≥ 47px when simulating iOS chrome.

## Touch & accessibility

- Minimum tap target: **44×44px** (prefer 48px for primary actions).
- Use semantic elements: `button`, `a`, `input`, `label`, `main`, `header`, `nav`.
- Interactive controls need visible `:focus-visible` styles.
- Color contrast ≥ WCAG AA for body text; note if placeholder contrast is intentionally lower.

## Structure for designer review

Prefer clear regions designers can map to Figma frames later:

```html
<main class="screen" data-screen="checkout-nudge">
  <header class="screen__header">...</header>
  <section class="screen__body">...</section>
  <footer class="screen__footer">...</footer>
</main>
```

- Use `data-state` attributes or classes for variant demos (`is-open`, `has-error`).
- Comment major sections in HTML for handoff readability.

## Interactions (MVP)

- Vanilla JS only; keep scripts inline at bottom of `<body>`.
- Demo interactions: sheet open/close, tab switch, fake form validation — no API calls.
- Prefer CSS transitions over heavy animation libraries.

## Versioning & iteration

- Semver in HTML comment: `1.0.0` initial, patch for fixes, minor for new states/sections.
- Mirror changelog in companion `*-notes.md` — never delete prior entries.
- When iterating, summarize "feedback addressed" in notes file.

## Typography & color

- Use system font stack unless brand fonts specified: `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif`.
- Define CSS custom properties for colors/spacing at `:root` for easy iteration.
- Document token names in notes even when not synced from a design token file.

## Do not

- Desktop-first layouts or min-width breakpoints above 390px as primary target.
- External CDN scripts (React, Tailwind) unless user explicitly requests.
- Lorem ipsum without labeling placeholder copy in notes open questions.
